{"n": 1243, "w": 1000, "h": 764, "img": "1243.webp", "text": "65-118\n\nTROUBELSHOOTING\n\nTroubleshooting should always begrn with an inspections of the antenna.\n\nROD ANTENNA / Antenna Length\n\nCHECKING ANTENNA\n\nThe ideo! antenna length for AM/FM reception is\nabout 0.9 to 1,0 meters (35 to 39”),\nIMPORTANT:\n\nThe bottom telescope section must always be\npulled out fully.\n\nCONNECTION:\n\nTune in a medium wave station.\n\nThe connection of the antenna is okay, if when\ncontacting the antenna rod the reception tures\nconsiderably quieter (at least difference in\nJoudness).\n\nGROUND CONNECTION:\n\nThe resistance measured between the antenna\nplug, ground terminal and body should be zero,\nUV this value is pot reached, the ground connec\nion on the antenna base and/or upper holder 1s\nhot correct,\n\nCURRENT FLOW\n\nThe current flow rewstance measured between\nthe antenna plug peak and antenna rod should\nbe zero ohms, and never above 3 ohms. To\ncheck for breaks, the antenna wire must ber\nmoved continuouily while measuring the rows\nlance.\n\nIMPORTANT!\nNot applicable to extension wire due to short\nening capacitor\n\nINSULATION RESISTANCE\n\nIM the insulation resistance between the antenna\nplug peak and plug ground terminal is less than\n1 Mobm, the antenna or antenna wire has\nground out and must be replaced.\n\nSERVICING\n\nClean a pulled out antenna rod often with a dry\ncloth and then coat with an antenna grease\".\nThis 1s especially important after long ting in\n\nram.\n\n* Source HWE", "words": [["65-118", 0.4682, 0.0204, 0.5383, 0.0442], ["TROUBELSHOOTING", 0.188, 0.0699, 0.2999, 0.0818], ["Troubleshooting", 0.0176, 0.1029, 0.0968, 0.1161], ["should", 0.1013, 0.0989, 0.1285, 0.1201], ["always", 0.1336, 0.0989, 0.1648, 0.1201], ["begrn", 0.1689, 0.0989, 0.192, 0.1201], ["with", 0.1971, 0.0989, 0.2172, 0.1201], ["an", 0.2213, 0.0989, 0.2308, 0.1201], ["inspections", 0.2359, 0.1016, 0.3009, 0.1148], ["of", 0.2923, 0.0989, 0.3019, 0.1201], ["the", 0.3